course: dictionary
lesson: 11807
title: Bewitched: under a spell, or charmed
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. Bewitched is one of them. In a fairy tale, «The witch bewitched the prince, and he turned into a frog» means he was put under a magic spell. Look at the clues: a witch, a prince, a frog. Those are magic clues.
explain: Bewitched can also mean charmed and delighted, as if by magic. «Ben stood bewitched by the music, and he forgot the time» does not mean a spell was cast. Ben was so captivated that he could not stop listening. The clue is that he forgot the time, because he was enjoying something beautiful.
explain: To choose the right meaning, ask: is there a witch, a wizard or a curse in the sentence? If yes, the magic spell meaning fits. If the sentence is about something lovely that holds someone's attention, the charmed meaning fits. Then try your meaning in the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
fact: Bewitched is the past form of the verb bewitch.
fact: «Bewitched» means under a magic spell put on by a witch or wizard.
fact: «Bewitched» can also mean charmed and delighted, as if by magic.
fact: In The Wind in the Willows, Mole is bewitched by the river, and Toad seems bewitched by motor cars.
fact: Context clues, like a witch or a beautiful song, help you pick the right meaning of a word with more than one sense.
exercise: «The wicked witch bewitched the prince, and he turned into a frog.» What does bewitched mean here? | Hungry for dinner | Covered in mud | Tired after a long walk | *Under a magic spell
exercise: «Ben stood bewitched by the music.» What does bewitched mean here? | *Charmed and delighted, as if by magic | Angry about the noise | Bored and yawning | Hungry for dinner
exercise: Mole sat bewitched by the river all afternoon. What does bewitched show about Mole? | Lost in a wood | Bored and ready to go home | *Completely captured by the river, as if under a spell | Frightened of the water
test: The princess was bewitched by the witch and could not wake up. What does bewitched mean? | Hungry for supper | Covered in paint | *Under a magic spell | Very tired after a long walk
test: Ahmed was bewitched by the sunset and forgot to go home. What does bewitched mean here? | Sleepy and yawning | Scared of the dark | *Charmed and delighted, as if by magic
exam: Which sentence uses bewitched to mean charmed by something beautiful? | *«Ruby was bewitched by the glowing lights of the night market.» | «The bus was late this morning.» | «The mouse ate the cheese quickly.» | «The sun was hot at noon.»
